@section Performance Comparison
@cindex Performance Comparison

This section compares flexichain performance with other sequence data structures for common operations.

@subsection Insertion Performance

@lisp
(module performance-comparison (library flexichain))

;; Compare insertion at beginning
(define (benchmark-insertions n)
   ;; Flexichain (gap buffer)
   (let ((chain (make-gapbuffer))
         (start-time (current-time)))
      (do ((i 0 (+ i 1)))
          ((= i n))
          (flexi-insert! chain 0 i))
      (let ((flexi-time (- (current-time) start-time)))
         
         ;; Vector (for comparison)
         (set! start-time (current-time))
         (let ((vec (make-vector 0)))
            (do ((i 0 (+ i 1)))
                ((= i n))
                ;; Simulate vector insertion (expensive)
                (let ((new-vec (make-vector (+ i 1))))
                   (vector-copy! new-vec 1 vec 0 i)
                   (vector-set! new-vec 0 i)
                   (set! vec new-vec))))
         (let ((vector-time (- (current-time) start-time)))
            
            ;; List (for comparison)  
            (set! start-time (current-time))
            (let ((lst '()))
               (do ((i 0 (+ i 1)))
                   ((= i n))
                   (set! lst (cons i lst))))
            (let ((list-time (- (current-time) start-time)))
               
               (print "Insertions for " n " elements:")
               (print "  Flexichain: " flexi-time "ms")
               (print "  Vector:     " vector-time "ms") 
               (print "  List:       " list-time "ms")))))

;; Run benchmark
(benchmark-insertions 1000)
@end lisp

@subsection Expected Performance Characteristics

@table @strong
@item Flexichain (Gap Buffer)
@itemize @bullet
@item Insertion/deletion at gap: O(1) amortized
@item Insertion/deletion elsewhere: O(n) worst case, but gap moves to frequently accessed positions
@item Random access: O(1)
@item Memory overhead: Low, single contiguous buffer
@end itemize

@item Vector
@itemize @bullet  
@item Insertion/deletion at end: O(1) amortized
@item Insertion/deletion elsewhere: O(n) always
@item Random access: O(1)
@item Memory overhead: Low
@end itemize

@item List
@itemize @bullet
@item Insertion/deletion at head: O(1)
@item Insertion/deletion elsewhere: O(n) to find position
@item Random access: O(n)
@item Memory overhead: High due to pointer storage
@end itemize
@end table

@subsection When to Use Flexichain

Flexichain is ideal when you need:

@itemize @bullet
@item
Frequent insertions and deletions at varying positions
@item
Random access to elements by position
@item
Cursor-based editing operations
@item
Position-aware elements (ranked flexichains)
@item
Memory-efficient sequence storage
@end itemize

Common use cases include:
@itemize @bullet
@item Text editors and word processors
@item Syntax analyzers and parsers  
@item Document object models
@item Undo/redo systems
@item Interactive sequence manipulation
@end itemize
